# The HUD menu's Battery Cell Voltage: off, it asks "Cell Count" from 4 and draws the battery's
# voltage over that count - "Cell 4.20v" - on the HUD's lower bottom line, the battery line moved
# up above it; a count that is not a whole number is the C#'s "Bad Radius"; on, a click turns the
# line off without asking.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:6229-6254, ExtLibs/Controls/HUD.cs:2848-2920`
#
# Needs SITL (a copter, whose battery reads about 12.6 V): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-hudcells.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 12

expect fly.hud.cells off
expect fly.hud.cell none

# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click hud@0.5x0.4:right
expect fly.hud.menu true
click fly-hud-batterycells
expect fly.hud.menu false
expect fly.prompt Cell Count
expect fly.prompt.value 4
key ctrl+u
type four
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect status Error: Bad Radius
expect fly.hud.cells off

# Cancel leaves it off.
click hud@0.5x0.4:right
click fly-hud-batterycells
click fly-prompt-cancel
expect fly.hud.cells off

click hud@0.5x0.4:right
click fly-hud-batterycells
key ctrl+u
type 3
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.hud.cells 3
expect fly.hud.cell ~ Cell 4.

click hud@0.5x0.4:right
click fly-hud-batterycells
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.hud.cells off
expect fly.hud.cell none
